{
  "description": "Pairing a box by the code it shows (protocol/adoption.md section 7, RFC 0001 Amendment 8). cpace_b1 and cpace_low_order are draft-irtf-cfrg-cpace-14's Appendix B.1 and B.1.10 (CPACE-X25519-SHA512), copied from the draft: generator, Ya, Yb, K and ISK must come out as printed, and every low-order u-coordinate must give its q (all zeros: abort). run is this project's whole exchange with fixed scalars, sid and pair id: the generator from the code and CI = lv_cat(\"atalaia pair v1\", pair id), ADa \"atalaia controller\", ADb \"atalaia box\", the keys from the ISK (HKDF-SHA256, salt = sid), the tags, the join key sealed with AES-128-CCM (8-byte MIC) and the five frames; wrong_code is the box's answer when it shows another code. generators are codes, pair ids and sids whose hashed generator string is 2^254 or more (r_high) or below, with their generator g. invalid lists bodies and frames every codec must refuse.",
